WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.860
Speaker 1: Well, I told you yesterday that
we would be looking at this today.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:08.820
The rehabilitation, for lack of a better term
of the Biden presidency that's happened over

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.139
a period of just 26 days is quite stunning.

00:00:12.139 --> 00:00:15.290
Think back to 26 days, almost a month ago.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:18.680
Gas prices were down a little bit, but not
really that much.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:23.090
We had just gotten yet another higher inflation
report.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:29.300
Joe Biden had had a significant lag time in
terms of major legislative accomplishments

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.980
during his presidency.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:34.440
And many were saying, what is the game plan
here?

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.370
What is the justification for voting for Democrats
in November?

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:41.340
What's the justification for thinking it's
even remotely plausible that Joe Biden might

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:46.650
run for reelection in November or in November
of 2024, that is.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:51.980
And you had a relatively strong, strong Trump
doing rallies, surging, searching, still with

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:55.630
quite a high favorability rating among Republicans.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:01:03.650
And think about the last 26 days where we
have now seen a significant not yet explosive

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:08.760
but significant, very decided uptick in Joe
Biden's approval rating.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.350
If you take a look at the numbers, you see
that the approval rating for Joe Biden bottomed

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:16.720
out right around July 20, July 21.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.390
That was kind of the low point now closing
in on about a month ago.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:29.330
And since then, it has been a decidedly positive
trend, not so much in terms of the numbers.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:32.909
I mean, it's really just been a shift from
37 to 40.

00:01:32.909 --> 00:01:39.240
But remember that these are averages among
many different polls and the direction is

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.630
clearly positive compared to past presidents.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:48.770
You might remember that FiveThirtyEight has
this great tool where you can compare Joe

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:54.620
Biden's current approval rating to those of
past presidents at this point in time, I believe,

00:01:54.620 --> 00:02:03.630
were 574 days into Joe Biden's presidency,
and it was below every single president dating

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.920
all the way back to Truman.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.780
It's now not quite so bad if you compare it
to prior presidents.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:14.870
Joe Biden's uptick is now putting himself
within striking distance of where Donald Trump

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:17.340
was at this point in his presidency.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:24.920
If you look at Bill Clinton with just a couple
more points, Biden would now have an equivalent

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:28.350
approval rating to that of Bill Clinton at
this point in his presidency.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.840
You look at Reagan basically the same.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:34.620
That gap where Reagan was more popular at
this point in his presidency has essentially

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:35.620
been eliminated.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:42.360
And Biden has almost caught up there of roughly
equal to Jimmy Carter and now above.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:43.360
Harry Truman.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:44.490
Harry Truman.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:49.390
A very low approval rating at this point in
his presidency, only 33 and Joe Biden above

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.390
that.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.040
So what is the reason for this change?

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.690
Well, it's a combination of things.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:59.470
It's some good news for Joe Biden and really
just humiliating bad news for Republicans

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:00.680
and for Donald Trump.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:07.370
If you look at the Biden side, the positive
side, Inflation Reduction Act, Pact Act, a

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:13.660
jobs report with more than twice the number
of new jobs created versus the expectation

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:18.620
a wage report wages up half of a percent in
July.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:24.020
Inflation report inflation year over year
coming down for the 12 month period ending

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.540
on July 31st.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:31.200
And yes, although admittedly controversial
among progressives, the strike that successfully

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:38.500
killed al Qaeda terrorist Ayman al-Zawahiri,
no due process of concern to many down on

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.500
the left.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.989
We will talk about that on the Thursday show.

00:03:41.989 --> 00:03:48.370
But as far as presidential accomplishments
tend to go, taking out a known terrorist on

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:53.430
the most wanted list, generally speaking,
is considered an accomplishment.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:56.320
And I know everybody will get mad and everybody
emails me as is David.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:57.500
How can you call that an accomplishment?

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.440
How could you gloat about that?

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:00.900
It might not even be legal.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:01.989
I'm with you.

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:02.989
I'm with you.

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:06.760
But as far as presidential accomplishments
are concerned, it certainly counts.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:12.489
So Joe Biden doing significant, significantly
much to help himself.

00:04:12.489 --> 00:04:16.449
And then also you look at what's happening
on the Republican side.

00:04:16.449 --> 00:04:21.989
Donald Trump now under criminal investigation
for violating the Espionage Act among a number

00:04:21.989 --> 00:04:24.030
of other different federal statutes.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:29.789
His home, Mar-A-Lago, having a search warrant
served, tons of stuff taken.

00:04:29.789 --> 00:04:34.810
We learned yesterday that Trump's former personal
lawyer, Rudy Giuliani, is now under criminal

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:36.750
investigation in Georgia.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:41.189
We learned yesterday that Donald Trump's Trump
Organization, CFO Allen Weisselberg is getting

00:04:41.189 --> 00:04:44.240
ready to take a guilty plea.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:48.069
It's it's all very, very bad on the Trump
side.

00:04:48.069 --> 00:04:53.219
So all of a sudden, you have the midterms
not looking so bad with Democrats now, not

00:04:53.219 --> 00:04:56.850
by much, but slightly favored to take the
Senate.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:57.979
Democrats still like.

00:04:57.979 --> 00:05:04.389
To lose the house, but maybe by not very much,
and at least a reinvigorated Democratic electorate.

00:05:04.389 --> 00:05:07.139
Now, what will actually happen in November?

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:12.740
And what is the viability of Trump and or
Biden to run in 2024?

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:19.849
Still unclear, but a dramatic, dramatic turnaround
from where things were certainly 60 days ago.

00:05:19.849 --> 00:05:26.819
Oh, and gas prices, I forgot to mention gas
prices also yesterday or today, ending something

00:05:26.819 --> 00:05:30.199
like a 65 consecutive day decline.

00:05:30.199 --> 00:05:35.009
All of those things are good as far as the
presidency is concerned.

00:05:35.009 --> 00:05:40.289
And yeah, I mean, listen, it's a reasonable
thing to make the case that actually higher

00:05:40.289 --> 00:05:45.699
gas prices, in a sense, are good long term
because they encourage people to abandon gasoline

00:05:45.699 --> 00:05:46.699
powered vehicles.

00:05:46.699 --> 00:05:49.830
You're 100% correct, if that's your view.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:55.159
But the narrative is the very high gas prices
are a negative indicator for the economy.

00:05:55.159 --> 00:05:57.080
Gas prices coming down are a good thing.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:03.430
And so we have to analyze these things not
so much in the full depth that you and I might,

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:08.149
but in terms of how it is perceived as far
as a presidency goes and a very good 26 days

00:06:08.149 --> 00:06:09.149
for Joe Biden, will it continue?

00:06:09.149 --> 00:06:09.620
We don't know, but we will follow it.

